# Admin-plane gateway origin the Google sign-in start handler redirects to.
# This is the Go backend — a SEPARATE origin from this frontend.
# Staging: https://staging-gw.prismsek.com    Prod: https://api.prismsek.com
# Server-only (never exposed to the browser). For local dev, copy to .env.local.
GATEWAY_ORIGIN=https://staging-gw.prismsek.com

# Where Google sign-in returns the browser is a BACKEND setting, not ours: we
# hand the gateway an internal return path (/sign-in/callback?n=<nonce>) and it
# prepends its own PSK_CONSOLE_URL. For the browser to land back on THIS
# frontend, the Go backend must run with PSK_CONSOLE_URL=https://app.prismsek.com
# — its default "" yields a relative redirect back to the gateway origin, and the
# console.prismsek.com in the backend's deploy/.env.example is a different origin.
# Sending an absolute return URL from here instead is rejected by the gateway's
# open-redirect guard (isInternalPath), which would drop the nonce and break sign-in.
